  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_racial_slur",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Racial slur via phonetic mimicry",
  "description": "The top panel mocks the pronunciation of '1-800-abos-r-dum' as a racial slur by juxtaposing it with an image of a person in Native American regalia. This is a form of racial stereotyping that uses phonetic mimicry to imply that the Black man in the bottom panel is also being mocked for his race, reinforcing a hateful message. The use of 'abos-r-dum' as a slur is a real-world reference to the racial slur 'nigger' (phonetically similar to 'nigga' or 'nigger'), which is a deeply offensive and racist term.",
